//   1) Scale C by beta in a cache- and vector-friendly traversal.
//   2) Perform the matrix product using a k-i-j traversal:
//        for k
//          for i
//            let aik = alpha * A[i,k]
//            for j
//              C[i,j] += aik * B[k,j]
//
//   This order improves data locality for B's rows and keeps the innermost loop
//   over j, which is contiguous in all three matrices.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
